TITLE: Game based methodologies. Active learning for professional&#13;
development. ABSTRACT:&#13;
The present contribution describes three learning methodologies based on game:&#13;
gamification, lego serious play and serious game. It analyzes examples of these&#13;
methodologies within learning and working contexts. It describes examples of real&#13;
and virtual environments enhanced by game mechanics and dynamics. Game-based&#13;
methodologies (GBM) proposing connections between learning and action, facilitate&#13;
reflection and change that are key elements for professional development. The&#13;
engaging, collaborative and sometimes competitive nature of these learning&#13;
methodologies open up new paths for learning, proposing strategies and&#13;
interventions for educational settings that enhance professional practice and&#13;
experience.
